# Generic synthesis of nb_dcache_top (open-source yosys flow).
# Input is sv2v-converted Verilog (yosys' native parser can't take the rich SV).
#
# The tag and (especially) data arrays are SYNCHRONOUS-read, so memory_collect
# keeps them as $mem cells -- SRAM-mappable storage -- instead of lowering them
# to flip-flops. `stat` reports the inferred memories (the 16 KiB data array
# becomes a single memory) plus the control-logic cell count. (We stop before
# memory_dff/abc, which are slow on the wide data port in this open flow; an
# SRAM-targeted backend would map the $mem cells to compiled macros.)
read_verilog -sv nb_dcache_synth.v
hierarchy -top nb_dcache_top
proc
memory_collect
opt -fast
stat
